      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Tutankhamun's Death</strong><br>\nTutankhamun died young, around 18 or 19 years old, and the cause of his death remains a subject of debate. Some theories suggest he died from an accident, illness, or even murder. His premature death meant his own tomb was not ready, and he was buried in a smaller tomb that was likely intended for someone else.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Tutankhamun's Tomb</strong><br>\nTutankhamun's tomb is located in the Valley of the Kings and was designated KV62. The tomb's layout was smaller than that of other pharaohs, reflecting the unexpected nature of his death. The artifacts found within the tomb have given historians insight into the opulence and artistry of ancient Egypt.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Tutankhamun's Mask</strong><br>\nThe most famous artifact from Tutankhamun's tomb is his funerary mask. Made of gold and adorned with colored glass and semiprecious stones, the mask has become an icon of ancient Egypt. It exemplified the Egyptian mastery of art and the significance they placed on the afterlife.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
