          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Curse of the Pharaohs</strong><br>\nThe supposed \"Curse of the Pharaohs\" is a legend that arose from the deaths of some individuals connected to the tomb's discovery. However, many of those involved, including Howard Carter, lived long lives, and the curse is widely regarded as a myth without scientific basis.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Tutankhamun's Legacy</strong><br>\nTutankhamun is one of the most well-known pharaohs, and his legacy lives on through the artifacts found in his tomb. His short life and the mystery surrounding his death continue to fascinate both scholars and the public, making him a subject of enduring interest.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Modern Interest in Tutankhamun</strong><br>\nThe modern interest in Tutankhamun has not waned, with exhibitions of his tomb's artifacts drawing large crowds worldwide. His life and death provide insight into the politics, culture, and religious beliefs of ancient Egypt, keeping the young pharaoh's memory alive today.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
